{"id":8,"frontend_id":8,"title":"Array Subset","slug":"array-subset","difficulty":"Easy","pattern_category":"arrays","tags":["arrays","dataset"],"company_tags":["Apple"],"ac_rate":"82.6%","statement":"Given two arrays of integers, arr1 and arr2, determine if arr2 is a subset of arr1. \n   Return 1 if arr2 is a subset of arr1, otherwise return 0. \n   An array arr2 is a subset of array arr1 if each element of arr2 is also an element of arr1. \n   \n   ## Constraints \n   - -10^5 \u2264 arr1[i], arr2[i] \u2264 10^5 \n   - 1 \u2264 arr1.length, arr2.length \u2264 10^5\n\n### Examples\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** `arr1 = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], arr2 = [1, 2, 3]`\n\n**Output:** `[]`\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** `arr1 = [10, 20, 30], arr2 = [20, 30, 40]`\n\n**Output:** `[]`\n","hints":[],"starter_code_python":"class Solution: \n       def solve(self, arr1: list, arr2: list) -> int: \n           # Convert arr1 to a set for efficient lookups \n           set1 = set(arr1) \n           # Check if all elements of arr2 are in set1 \n           for num in arr2: \n               if num not in set1: \n                   return 0 \n           return 1","example_test_cases":[{"stdin":"{\"arr1\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], \"arr2\": [1, 2, 3]}","expected_stdout":"[]","is_hidden":false,"order":0},{"stdin":"{\"arr1\": [10, 20, 30], \"arr2\": [20, 30, 40]}","expected_stdout":"[]","is_hidden":false,"order":1}],"hidden_test_cases":[{"stdin":"{\"arr1\": [1, 1, 1], \"arr2\": [1]}","expected_stdout":"[]","is_hidden":true,"order":2},{"stdin":"{\"arr1\": [5, 10, 15, 20], \"arr2\": [5, 15]}","expected_stdout":"[]","is_hidden":true,"order":3},{"stdin":"{\"arr1\": [-1, -2, -3], \"arr2\": [-1, -2]}","expected_stdout":"[]","is_hidden":true,"order":4},{"stdin":"{\"arr1\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], \"arr2\": [6, 7, 8]}","expected_stdout":"[]","is_hidden":true,"order":5},{"stdin":"{\"arr1\": [10, 20, 30, 40, 50], \"arr2\": [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]}","expected_stdout":"[]","is_hidden":true,"order":6},{"stdin":"{\"arr1\": [1, 